All 15 tests pass. Here's a summary of the 10 bugs fixed across 3 source files:

**`src/auth.py`** (2 bugs):
- `has_permission` — wasn't case-insensitive; added `.lower()` comparison
- `is_admin_or_owner` — used `and` instead of `or`; a user needed to be *both* admin *and* owner to get access

**`src/inventory.py`** (4 bugs):
- `__init__` — mutable default `{}` shared across all instances (classic Python gotcha); switched to `None`
- `add` — overwrote stock with `=` instead of accumulating with `+=`
- `reserve` — used `>=` instead of `>` so reserving exactly available stock raised `OutOfStock`
- `release` — didn't guard against releasing more than reserved, allowing negative reserved counts

**`src/text_utils.py`** (4 bugs):
- `slugify` — didn't lowercase characters; added `.lower()`
- `slugify` — `replace("--", "-")` only collapsed one pair of consecutive dashes; replaced with `re.sub(r"-+", "-")`
- `truncate` — sliced at `text[:max_len]` then appended suffix, producing `max_len + len(suffix)`; needed `text[:max_len - len(suffix)]`
